perf: build on node:25-bookworm-slim

The full node image carries ~950 MB of build toolchain this image never
uses -- a 588 MB apt layer among others. The runtime is `node
serveronly`, and the only build-time package needed is gettext, which
the Dockerfile already installs explicitly.

Measured on amd64:

  node:25-bookworm       2.13 GB
  node:25-bookworm-slim  1.18 GB   (-950 MB, 45%)

Verified at parity rather than assumed: both images report node v25.9.0,
carry /usr/bin/envsubst, resolve an identical 658 packages under
MagicMirror/node_modules, and have both source patches applied (the
/health route in js/server.js and the --require ./otel-init.js rewrite
in package.json).

Found while investigating ci-pool node failures: this build was writing
37.7 GB to a 41.66 GB node and taking kubelet and CRI-O down with it,
evicting every other pod on the node. This change is worth making on its
own merits but does NOT fix that -- a 2.13 GB image writing 37.7 GB is a
~17x amplification in buildkit's on-disk state, which is tracked
separately in docs/projects/ci-build-disk-exhaustion.md.

